Now the metaphysical
implications of thinkers

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:08.881
like Thacker and Brassiere would of course

00:11:08.881 --> 00:11:12.640
be ideal reading for Jobu and
the bagel gang's book group.

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:15.680
They basically confirmed
Jobu's nihilistic metaphysics

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:20.240
by arguing that the cosmos
is a cold, uncaring nothing,

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.570
and that life has mostly pain and despair

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.670
with a few little moments of happiness

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:25.980
sprinkled here and there.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:27.490
And like we already said,

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:28.660
at a certain point,

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.290
it seems like Evelyn wants in

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.584
on the book group as well.

00:11:31.584 --> 00:11:33.820
But she snaps out of it due to Waymond's

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:35.590
simple but effective plea

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:38.621
for everyone to just be kind.

00:11:38.621 --> 00:11:40.223
- The only thing I do know,

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.790
is that we have to be kind.

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:47.250
And while this could strike
some as corny and reductive,

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:50.490
as if being kind is a cure to large scale,

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:52.260
metaphysical meaninglessness,

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:54.830
it actually gets at something important.

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:57.020
Now for Thacker and Brassier,

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.380
pessimism and nihilism aren't
just existential principles.

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.970
But metaphysical and even scientific ones.

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:05.830
Because when everything
humanity has ever created,

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:09.100
is burned like a bagel left
in the toaster too long,

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:12.490
nothing we will have ever
done is really gonna matter.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:14.710
And all attempts to find
happiness and purpose

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:18.100
in the meantime, are
equivalent to closing your eyes

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.470
and listening to a mildly
interesting podcast

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:23.200
as your plane hurdles towards the ground.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:26.350
But this of course, isn't
where the Wayne family ends up.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:29.290
Evelyn, inspired by
Waymond's unceasing optimism

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.280
and calls for kindness
in the face of fear,

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:34.780
decides that existence is
something worth fighting for.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:37.110
And rather than using
your homicidal pinky's

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.300
to take out her enemies,

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.450
she responds with a love and kindness

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:42.880
that seems to target the fear and despair

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:44.630
motivating her opponents.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.350
And maybe, not surprisingly,

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:47.950
some recent French philosophers,

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.810
the children and grandchildren

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:51.480
of the existentialist so to speak,

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.610
are using the spirit of existentialism

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:56.820
to combat the metaphysics
of niahlist despair.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:58.300
Okay, so it's like this,

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:00.830
the existentialist
operated with the principal

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.170
that the true nature of reality

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:05.210
was basically unknowable.

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:08.560
And trying to understand it
would just make us miserable,

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:10.030
because we'd always experienced

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:12.810
the contradiction
between our subjectivity,

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.920
and the objective nature of reality.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.610
Instead, we should focus
on making decisions

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:21.230
and taking responsibility
for our own existence.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:23.380
And anyways, why worry about metaphysics

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:24.980
when you can drink martini's?

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:27.680
But contemporary philosophers
like Alain Badiou

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.110
and Quentin Meillassoux,
are both continuing

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:33.159
to embrace the power that
decisions play in existence,

00:13:33.159 --> 00:13:35.990
while also embracing metaphysics.

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:39.500
And while it's kind of a
lot of complicated stuff,

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.420
the just is, that while
the existentialists focus

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.730
on the inconsistency between reality,

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:46.420
and our attempts to understand it,

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:48.660
this newer crop of French smarties

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:53.660
identify that inconsistency as
a feature of reality itself.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:56.760
In one sense, it seems like
there is a lack of freedom

00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:59.380
in the everything everywhere
all at once multiverse,

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:02.930
as each version of Evelyn
seems borderline destined

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:05.470
to carry out a specific type of existence.

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:06.860
But Badiou would argue,

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.590
that while each of these universes

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:10.180
seems to have finite limits,

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.180
within each universe,
there is a trans finite

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:14.350
sense of possibility.

00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:16.760
Put simply, while we
would normally consider

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:19.150
the distance between
the numbers one and two

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:20.630
to be a finite limit,

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:21.930
within that limit,

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.860
there's an infinite amount of numbers,

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:28.473
i.e., 1.0, 1.34, 1.5,
1.0009804356, et cetera.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:33.760
In existential terms,

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.930
this means that even if we're caught

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:38.510
in a certain finite condition, i.e.,

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:39.910
we have hot dogs for fingers,

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:42.004
we still have infinite possibilities

00:14:42.004 --> 00:14:43.920
within those conditions.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:47.020
I.e., we can learn to play
the piano with our feet.

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:50.110
For Badiou, this means that
novel things can happen

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:52.410
in seemingly finite situations.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.650
And when these things
happen under what he calls

00:14:54.650 --> 00:14:56.159
the four conditions of truth,

00:14:56.159 --> 00:14:58.840
art, love, science, and politics,

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:01.000
we're capable of finding ideas

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.830
that can give our lives meaning.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.730
And these ideas share
something with existentialism,

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:07.630
and that we can't simply believe in them

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:09.730
like they're true or false,

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:12.070
rather, we need to take responsibility

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:14.100
for the consequences of these ideas

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:15.670
in our own lives.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:17.010
At the end of the film,

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:19.150
Evelyn and Joys futures aren't certain

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:20.680
just because they've decided

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.670
to avoid anniahlation by bagel.

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:23.890
They'll have to stay faithful

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:25.660
to their decision each day,

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:28.555
as they continue to find
meaning in their lives.

00:15:28.555 --> 00:15:30.220
And Meillassoux argues

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:33.720
that rather than reality
being either a chaotic,

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:36.780
meaningless mess, or a well ordered system

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:38.830
of necessary truth and causation,

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:42.390
it is both contingent and necessary.

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:46.260
Or as he puts it, "The only
necessity is contingency."

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:48.970
To put it in terms a raccoon
chef could understand,

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:51.240
it's not that reality doesn't make sense

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.490
because we're not capable
of understanding it,

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:56.790
it's that reality simply
doesn't make sense

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.750
in a clearly logical way.

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:02.010
It's basically a metaphysics
reverse engineered

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:03.610
out of existentialism.

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:05.680
And this view of reality seems to be there

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:07.010
in the scene in the movie.

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:09.650
That really made me cry a lot.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:14.650
Here, all we get are a few specks of time

00:16:14.877 --> 00:16:18.244
where any of this
actually makes any sense.

00:16:18.244 --> 00:16:19.890
- [Narrator] Here, Evelyn and Jobu

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:23.160
are able to acknowledge that
reality doesn't make sense,

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.610
and at the same time,

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:26.250
there is space for them to create

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.610
their own meaning and purpose.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:33.390
- That I will cherish
these few specks of time.

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:34.842
- And everything everywhere all at once,

00:16:34.842 --> 00:16:37.380
seems to be saying precisely this;

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.610
that even though the universe doesn't have

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:42.050
any inherent sense of order or meaning,

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:43.360
that within the context

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:45.690
of these seemingly random contingencies,

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.930
we are capable of creating meaning.

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:50.330
And when we get scared or feel stupid

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:53.280
because reality and existence
don't make sense to us,

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.380
problem isn't us.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:57.420
It's that reality itself
is kind of a mess.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:59.620
So does everything everywhere all at once,

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.000
end up confirming that

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.790
the universe is inherently meaningful,

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.600
and that if we just look hard enough,

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:07.560
meaning and truth will be
right there waiting for us?

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:08.830
Absolutely not.

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:12.110
But the film isn't coldly
embracing niahlism.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:14.260
Instead, it seems to be
taking the route of arguing

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:15.700
that just because reality

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:17.990
doesn't come pre-loaded with meaning,

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:21.860
doesn't mean that we can't
create truth in our own lives.

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:23.320
But what do you all think?

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:26.300
Is everything everywhere all
at once a necessary tonic

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:30.230
for a time when reality feels
pretty warped to begin with,

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:32.140
or were you just wondering
when the super heroes

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:33.110
were gonna show up?

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:34.640
Let us know in the comments.

